<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Babak Khorramdin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 795–838</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/papak">Babak</a> Khorramdin was the leader of the Khurramite revolt against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abbasid-caliphate">Abbasid Caliphate</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/azerbaijan">Azerbaijan</a> and western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>, which lasted from about 816 to 837. From his mountain stronghold of Badhdh he defeated several caliphal armies until the general Afshin took the fortress in 837. Handed over to the Abbasids by the Armenian prince <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sahl-smbatean">Sahl Smbatean</a>, he was executed at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samarra">Samarra</a> in 838.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/babak-khorramdin.jpg" alt="Babak Khorramdin" width="292" height="390" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 16th century artist · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Illustrated_leaf_from_the_Tarikhnama_of_Abu_%27Ali_Muhammad_ibn_Muhammad_al-Bal%27ami;_Afshin_and_Babak_arriving_at_Samarra._Persia,_Safavid_dynasty,_16th_century_(Babak_detail).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
